# O11-SHELL acceptance (independent oracles, written from the brief before the implementation exists).
# Every check below is expected to PASS on the finished outcome; there are no "!" known failures, so a failing line is a real gap.
# On main 2.5.0 (70db15e) 29 of them fail on purpose: a text AlertDialog for shortcuts, the first Tab lands in the header,
# Rooms covers 27% of a 1440x900 window on first run, Change… is a text list without the unavailable scene, Now with
# no room keeps the previous room's loop, and no CHANGELOG entry. G1-G3 (N13 Listen chips and station card) and B4
# already pass on main: O10 fixed the chip and card ellipsizing, and B4's baselines are main's own measurements.
A0 precondition: no room and no history (a first run)
A1 at 1200x800 the first run opens on Rooms with nothing focused in the header
A2 at 1200x800 the first Tab press lands on the first room card or the hero's primary action, not in the header
A3 at 1200x800 moving focus onto a card is inert: no command, no preview, nothing starts
A2 at 1200x800 the first Down press lands on the first room card or the hero's primary action, not in the header
A2 at 1200x800 the first Right press lands on the first room card or the hero's primary action, not in the header
A1 at 1440x900 the first run opens on Rooms with nothing focused in the header
A2 at 1440x900 the first Tab press lands on the first room card or the hero's primary action, not in the header
A3 at 1440x900 moving focus onto a card is inert: no command, no preview, nothing starts
A2 at 1440x900 the first Down press lands on the first room card or the hero's primary action, not in the header
A2 at 1440x900 the first Right press lands on the first room card or the hero's primary action, not in the header
B1 at 1440x900 on first run the Rooms content fills at least 45% of the window (share @@)
B2 at 1440x900 no card is cut off at the sides and no room name is ellipsized
B3 at 360 px the cards show whole across, with their names not ellipsized
B4 at 600 px the Rooms content share is not below main's (share @@)
B5 at 600 px no card is cut off at the sides and no room name is ellipsized
B4 at 700 px the Rooms content share is not below main's (share @@)
B5 at 700 px no card is cut off at the sides and no room name is ellipsized
B4 at 800 px the Rooms content share is not below main's (share @@)
B5 at 800 px no card is cut off at the sides and no room name is ellipsized
C0 precondition: Ctrl+? is the shortcuts action's accelerator
C1 Keyboard shortcuts opens an Adw.ShortcutsDialog (not a text alert)
C2 every application accelerator (each window action with a key) is listed
C3 every key of the window's shortcut controllers (Listen: Ctrl+F, Ctrl+L, Ctrl+V) is listed
C4 the keys handled by key controllers are listed (Space, Esc, Up, Down)
C5 the Rooms card options key (Menu or Shift+F10) is listed
C6 the dialog lists no key that nothing installs (the reserved Mix keys aside)
C7 every row has a title
C8 rows are grouped by page: more than one titled section, the Listen keys under a Listen section and the volume keys under a Now section
C9 the dialog is the same when opened again and from a second window, with no duplicate rows
C10 one shortcut table: each installed Ctrl shortcut is written in one statement of the source (source text)
C11 the table reserves the O11-CONTROL Mix keys (M, A, Shift+Up/Down) with a comment (source text)
D0 precondition: a room with its own scene is active, and one room scene is unavailable
D1 Scene › Change… shows a tile for every room scene, the unavailable one included
D2 each tile shows its own scene's card poster as a thumbnail
D3 thumbnails are card-sized (at most 640 px wide), not full posters
D4 the thumbnails form a grid (more than one per row, more than one row)
D5 the current scene's tile is marked: it differs from every other available tile (not by focus)
D6 the unavailable scene's tile is visibly unavailable (insensitive, dimmed or saying so)
D7 keyboard: a tile takes focus and Right moves it to another scene tile
D8 browsing the grid is inert: no command, no backend call, no new loop playing, no video in a tile
D9 activating the unavailable scene changes nothing
D10 Enter on another scene's tile changes the scene to it
D11 ... and only the scene: music and ambience are untouched and nothing starts
D12 reopened, the mark is on the newly chosen scene
D13 closing the grid without choosing sends nothing
E0 control: with a room, Now shows that room's scene art (the detector sees it)
E1 Now with no room and a video playing shows (precondition: Now is the page, Stop watching is there)
E2 ... a neutral state: no room's scene art and no loop on Now (left the room while on Now)
E3 a new window over the same no-room video: Now is neutral too
E4 entering a room afterwards shows its scene art again
G1 at 560 px no Listen scope chip is ellipsized
G2 at 560 px the station cards show whole names and Tune in (nothing ellipsized)
G3 at 560 px a station card's detail line is never cut inside its first word
G1 at 600 px no Listen scope chip is ellipsized
G2 at 600 px the station cards show whole names and Tune in (nothing ellipsized)
G3 at 600 px a station card's detail line is never cut inside its first word
G1 at 640 px no Listen scope chip is ellipsized
G2 at 640 px the station cards show whole names and Tune in (nothing ellipsized)
G3 at 640 px a station card's detail line is never cut inside its first word
G1 at 700 px no Listen scope chip is ellipsized
G2 at 700 px the station cards show whole names and Tune in (nothing ellipsized)
G3 at 700 px a station card's detail line is never cut inside its first word
K16r returning user (a last room, nothing active): Rooms with the hero button focused, nothing started
B6 at 1440x900 for a returning user (hero shown) the Rooms content fills at least 45% of the window (share @@)
H1 CHANGELOG records the change above 2.5.0 and mentions the keyboard shortcuts and the scene choice
